+### Sub-shape C: one HTML file, published as an Artifact
+
+Use this when the app has no page to host the variants yet, as when the prototype decides what those pages will look like. Use it too when the user will review away from the dev server, such as on a phone. Build one HTML file with each variant as a `<section class="variant" id="KEY" hidden>`, and paste in [switcher.html](switcher.html), which is the bottom bar for this sub-shape. It keys the variant on `location.hash`, because an Artifact link passes only a plain `#name`, never a query string. Fill the variants with the project's real content: its docs' example records, its fixtures, its wording. Publish the file as an Artifact and give the user a link per variant (`<url>#KEY`). Variants added later in the conversation go on the end of the list, so the numbers the user already uses keep naming the same variant.
+
+In every sub-shape the floating bottom bar works the same way.
 
